<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8" /><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" /><meta name="theme-color" content="#0b0d10" /><meta name="description" content="About Valentín Liñeiro — software engineer, architect, and builder interested in reducing friction and improving the way systems are built." /><title>About · Valentín Liñeiro</title></head>
<body><main><header><a class="brand" href={base}><img src={`${base}brand/takt.svg`} alt="" width="18" height="18"/>Valentín Liñeiro</a><nav><a href={`${base}archive/`}>Archive</a><a class="active" href={`${base}about/`}>About</a></nav></header>
<article><p class="eyebrow">About</p><h1>Software, systems, and the space between them.</h1><div class="bio"><p><strong>Valentín Liñeiro — Software engineer, 10+ years building backend systems, architectures and developer tooling.</strong></p><p>I work at the intersection of architecture, developer experience and AI-assisted engineering. My focus is reducing friction, preserving good decisions, and building systems that remain changeable.</p><p><strong>Currently:</strong> Java · TypeScript · distributed systems · AI-assisted workflows<br/><strong>Interested in:</strong> architecture · DX · agentic workflows</p><p><strong>Selected work:</strong> <a href="https://github.com/valentinlineiro/takt">TAKT</a> · <a href="https://github.com/valentinlineiro/blog">this blog</a></p></div><div class="links"><a href="https://github.com/valentinlineiro">GitHub</a><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/valentinlineiro/">LinkedIn</a><a href={`${base}rss.xml`}>RSS</a></div></article>
<footer><a href={base}>← Home</a></footer></main></body></html>
